      },
      "source": [
        "There are several algorithms used in artificial intelligence, each serving different purposes and tasks. Here are some of the fundamental algorithms commonly used in AI:\n",
        "\n",
        "1. **Search Algorithms**:\n",
        "   - Breadth-First Search (BFS)\n",
        "   - Depth-First Search (DFS)\n",
        "   - A* Search Algorithm\n",
        "   - Greedy Best-First Search\n",
        "\n",
        "2. **Optimization Algorithms**:\n",
        "   - Gradient Descent\n",
        "   - Stochastic Gradient Descent (SGD)\n",
        "   - Genetic Algorithms\n",
        "\n",
        "3. **Supervised Learning Algorithms**:\n",
        "- classification\n",
        "- regression\n",
        "   - Linear Regression\n",
        "   - Logistic Regression\n",
        "   - Decision Trees\n",
        "   - Support Vector Machines (SVM)\n",
        "   - k-Nearest Neighbors (k-NN)\n",
        "   - Naive Bayes\n",
        "\n",
        "4. **Unsupervised Learning Algorithms**:\n",
        "   - K-Means Clustering\n",
        "   - Hierarchical Clustering\n",
        "   - Principal Component Analysis (PCA)\n",
        "   - Independent Component Analysis (ICA)\n",
        "   - Gaussian Mixture Models (GMM)\n",
        "\n",
        "5. **Reinforcement Learning Algorithms**:\n",
        "   - Q-Learning\n",
        "   - Deep Q-Networks (DQN)\n",
        "   - Policy Gradient Methods\n",
        "   - Actor-Critic Methods\n",
        "6. **Neural Network Architectures**:\n",
        "   - Perceptron\n",
        "   - Feedforward neural network\n",
        "   - Multi-Layer Perceptron (MLP)\n",
        "   - Convolutional Neural Network (CNN)\n",
        "   - Recurrent Neural Network (RNN)\n",
        "   - Long Short-Term Memory (LSTM)\n",
        "   - Generative Adversarial Network (GAN)\n",
        "   - Transformer\n",
        "\n",
        "7. **Natural Language Processing (NLP) Algorithms**:\n",
        "   - Tokenization\n",
        "   - Stemming and Lemmatization\n",
        "   - Named Entity Recognition (NER)\n",
        "   - Word Embeddings (e.g., Word2Vec, GloVe)\n",
        "   - Sequence-to-Sequence Models (e.g., LSTM, GRU)\n",
        "\n",
        "8. **Computer Vision Algorithms**:\n",
        "   - Convolutional Neural Networks (CNNs)\n",
        "   - Haar Cascade Classifiers\n",
        "   - Histogram of Oriented Gradients (HOG)\n",
        "   - Feature Matching Algorithms (e.g., SIFT, SURF)\n",
        "   -RCNN, YOLO\n",
        "9. -llms, vlm, rags, agents, MCP\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "These basic algorithms form the building blocks of various AI applications and are used in combination or in isolation depending on the problem at hand and the specific requirements of the task. Additionally, advancements in AI research continually introduce new algorithms and techniques to improve the performance and capabilities of artificial intelligence systems."
